Today is Saturday evening.
I am going to Priya's house.
On the way, I see a bright sweet shop.
I think to myself that I will buy sweets here.
I enter the shop.
The shopkeeper is there.
I say to him, "Bhaiya, namaste."
I say, "I need half a kilo of Kaju Katli."
"Please pack it in a nice box."
The shopkeeper smiles.
He says, "Certainly, I will pack it in the box right now."
He puts the sweets in the box.
I ask, "What is the price?"
The shopkeeper says, "Five hundred rupees."
I give him five hundred rupees.
He gives me the box of sweets and the receipt.
I say thank you and leave the shop.
I think to myself, 'Now let's go to the metro station.'
I think to myself that Priya will be happy.
